WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
In 1967, a Christian philosopher began
working in multi-faith Birmingham.

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:12.520
He met devout Muslims, Sikhs, Hindus and Jews
whose lives seemed as holy as Christians'.

3
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.890
His name was John Hick.

4
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.420
He said theology needed
a Copernican revolution.

5
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:24.090
If every great religion changes lives,
could they all be paths to the same God?

6
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.810
In this mission, you'll
see Hick's new map,

7
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.020
with something he called
the Real at its centre.

8
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.750
Then you'll test his
idea against its critics,

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.400
and ask whether a Christian can hold it.

10
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.930
Your mission: weigh up whether every
great religion could be a path to the same

11
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.520
God.
